From 99a6fd0c02830b0ab50ea1112fd60224b0ea9bac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:26:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Share durable FIFO across flake owner and page
 retries

Pending-owner work previously ran before all existing pages. A slow failed owner lookup consumed every deadline and starved immutable retry pages despite per-queue rotation. Merge eligible work by shared durable tickets; retain pre-attempt rotation, exact readback and a deadline fence after batch flushes. Preserve bounded admission packing and retry-group boundaries; the half-window threshold flushes batches rather than imposing queue priority.

Proof: 608 tests passed across 23 consumer files. Ten exact-anchor mutants killed: both phase priorities, missing occurrence rotation/page delivery, stale and non-drain ticket filters, retry groups, post-flush deadline, pre-page flush and timed batch flush. Three original starvation assertions failed before implementation; composition also caught and fixed the 0/40 backlog regression. Full scripts/check: 20 checks OK. All fixtures disposable; no production queue or mini writes.
